From: wang lian <lianux.mm@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 16:34:27 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 8/8] mm/damon: upgrade SPE feedback with rbtree histogram
 and debugfs bridge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the PTE-only SPE prototype with a proper rbtree-based sub-page
access histogram that supports multiple data sources:

Data structure:
- Per-folio rbtree keyed by THP-aligned PFN
- Each entry tracks access_count[512] (one counter per 4KB subpage)
- Aging: entries older than 30s are pruned periodically

Two data source paths:
- Phase 2b (ready): userspace SPE daemon decodes ARM SPE records,
  feeds PFNs via debugfs (/sys/kernel/debug/damon/spe_feed)
- Phase 2c (requires hardware): kernel perf_event_create_kernel_counter
  for ARM SPE, overflow handler calls damon_spe_record_access()

Query path (unchanged flow, upgraded implementation):
- damon_spe_folio_heatmap() first checks the rbtree
- Falls back to PTE access bits if no SPE data available
- Returns -EOPNOTSUPP when neither source has data

New APIs:
- damon_spe_record_access(pfn, pid): record a single access
- damon_spe_prune(): remove stale entries (called from aggregation cycle)
- damon_spe_stats(): query rbtree statistics

The debugfs interface provides:
- /sys/kernel/debug/damon/spe_feed (write): accept one PFN per line
- /sys/kernel/debug/damon/spe_stats (read): show current histogram

This completes the Phase 2b data pipeline: userspace SPE daemon
decodes ARM SPE → feeds PFNs via debugfs → kernel rbtree →
damon_spe_folio_heatmap() → split decision.

